# mobsfscan configuration (https://github.com/MobSF/mobsfscan#configure-mobsfscan)
# Rules listed here are ACCEPTED RISKS, documented in SECURITY.md ("수용한 위험").
ignore-rules:
  # The app talks to a NAS on the local network; such servers are usually plain HTTP.
  # Cleartext is additionally gated at runtime by the "평문 HTTP 허용" setting (LrrAuthInterceptor).
  - android_manifest_base_config_cleartext
  # A NAS with a self-signed HTTPS certificate only works if the user-installed CA is trusted.
  # The user must deliberately install that CA on the device.
  - android_manifest_base_config_trust_user_certs
  # False positive: mobsfscan assumes targetSdk 26 when the manifest has no <uses-sdk> (AGP injects it
  # from build.gradle.kts where targetSdk = 35). The rule only applies to targetSdk < 29, and the
  # activity already sets taskAffinity="".
  - android_task_hijacking2
